# For AI agents

> **Blender researchers: stop here.** If your brief says you are researching Blender, ignore this file and everything it points to, and follow your brief alone. You may read your question sheet and the `Blender Sources/` folder — nothing else in this project. These documents are full of this project's own guesses about how Blender behaves, and reading them turns your findings into echoes that nobody downstream can tell apart from facts. That is the one failure the Blender Research stage cannot detect.

For everyone else: before doing anything in this project, open and read:

**`Preparation/Groundwork/Start Here.md`**

That file is the front door to how this project is planned and built — it points you to the rules, the glossary, and the conventions every agent must follow. Do not skip it. Do not rely on rules or conventions memorized from other projects; only the ones in Groundwork count here.

This file is only a signpost. It contains no rules of its own — all real rules live in Groundwork.
